    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Oak Ridge CDP spans northern Morris and western Passaic, including Oak Ridge proper on Pequannock River along Route 23 and the New York, Susquehanna & Western Railroad main line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Ridge%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "County Route 699, known locally as Oak Ridge Road, runs south from Route 23 and is the main north–south route in the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Ridge%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Pequannock River, forming the Passaic/Morris county line, winds through the CDP, separating Oak Ridge proper from Milton and Petersburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Ridge%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Oak Ridge Reservoir sits on the Pequannock near the northwest border, while several lakes—White Rock, Mitt, Moosepac, Cozy, Swannanoa, and Oak Ridge—drain into the Rockaway River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Ridge%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Green Pond Mountain, over 1,260 feet high, marks the southern border of Oak Ridge and the edge of Rockaway Township.",
